7.3,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.10301244955581601,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":84.9,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.03896758182031759,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":3,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":33.3,"_gate_spread":0.0042561824582639934,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":2.1,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.9996435748229272,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.008440622768625729,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":19.5,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.08615936945750981,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":4.6,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.048635737279791424,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":49.3,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.083661729795093,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":83.7,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.05279934540160428,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":69.8,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.0587504857930492,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0030657671459683013,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":94.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.25936002,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Covenant Logistics Group, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides transportation and logistics services in the United States. It operates through four segments: Expedited, Dedicated, Managed Freight, and Warehousing. The Expedited segment primarily provides truckload services with high service freight and delivery standards, such as 1,000 miles in 22 hours or 15-minute delivery windows. The Dedicated segment provides customers with committed truckload capacity over contracted periods with the goal of three to five years in length using equipment either owned or leased by the company. The Managed Freight segment offers brokerage services, including logistics capacity by outsourcing the carriage of customers' freight to third parties; and transport management services, such as logistics services on a contractual basis to customers who prefer to outsource their logistics needs. The Warehousing segment provides day-to-day warehouse management services to customers, as well as shuttle and switching services related to shuttling containers and trailers. The company also engages in used equipment sales and leasing business. It serves transportation companies, such as parcel freight forwarders, less-than-truckload carriers, and third-party logistics providers; and traditional truckload customers, including manufacturers, retailers, and food and beverage shippers. The company was formerly known as Covenant Transportation Group, Inc. and changed its name to Covenant Logistics Group, Inc. in May 2007. Covenant Logistics Group, Inc. was founded in 1986 and is based in Chattanooga, Tennessee.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David Ray Parker | Founder, CEO & Chairman | Age 67 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $402K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Covenant Logistics Group, Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $828M market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The company is burning through $34M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 0.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 5.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 26% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 354% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":3.5415214729505036},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Operating margins 9% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Industrials peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 8% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Valued at a 26% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"The Technical Signals Behind (CVLG) That Institutions Follow","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/150/The_Technical_Signals_Behind_CVLG_That_Institutions_Follow_111026034202_1794343322.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794343322.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Covenant Logistics Group (CVLG) vs. The Competition Financial Review","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/covenant-logistics-group-cvlg-vs-the-competition-financial-review.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794326330.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.844,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Covenant Logistics Group (NYSE:CVLG) Stock Jumps 10.3% \u2013 Time to Buy?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/02/covenant-logistics-group-nysecvlg-stock-jumps-10-3-time-to-buy.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793640072.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.836,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"CVLG Q3 deep dive: managed freight and dedicated contracts drive improvement amid transition costs","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/cvlg-q3-deep-dive-managed-102729334.html","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793442449.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.878,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","product"]},{"title":"Why Covenant Logistics (CVLG) stock is up today","source":"finance.yahoo.com